"round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M3 11.5 12 3.5l9 8M5.5 10v10.5h13V10M10 20.5V15h4v5.5"/></svg></span><span><strong>About 10,400</strong><span class="t">houses within half a mile of the ocean in Horry County</span></span></li><li><span class="i"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="20" height="20" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.75" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M3 11a9 7.5 0 0 1 18 0q-2.25-1.5-4.5 0t-4.5 0-4.5 0-4.5 0zM12 11v8M2.5 21.5c3-1.4 6.3-1.4 9.5 0s6.5 1.4 9.5 0"/></svg></span><span><strong>186 for sale</strong><span class="t">a 5-minute walk or less from a public beach path</span></span></li><li><span class="i"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="20" height="20" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.75" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M12 21s-7-6.2-7-11.5a7 7 0 0 1 14 0C19 14.8 12 21 12 21z"/><circle cx="12" cy="9.5" r="2.5"/></svg></span><span><strong>About every 250 to 400 feet</strong><span class="t">a public path to the sand in the beach towns</span></span></li></ul><style>.c3ph-f{position:relative;margin:0;border-radius:6px;overflow:hidden;background:var(--ivory-2)}.c3ph-f img{display:block;width:100%;height:auto;object-fit:cover}.c3ph-cr{position:absolute;right:0;bottom:0;max-width:100%;padding:1.6rem .6rem .35rem 2.6rem;font:400 .625rem/1.3 var(--sans);letter-spacing:.01em;color:#fff;text-align:right;background:radial-gradient(farthest-side at 100% 100%,rgba(28,32,40,.72),rgba(28,32,40,.4) 55%,rgba(28,32,40,0));white-space:nowrap;overflow:hidden;text-overflow:ellipsis;pointer-events:none}.c3ph-cr a{color:#fff;text-decoration:underline;text-decoration-color:rgba(255,255,255,.5);text-underline-offset:2px;pointer-events:auto;padding:10px 0 6px}.c3ph-hero{margin:1.6rem 0 2rem}.c3ph-hero .c3ph-f{border-radius:8px}.c3ph-hero img{aspect-ratio:4/3}@media (min-width:700px){.c3ph-hero img{aspect-ratio:16/9}}.c3ph-hero figcaption{color:var(--muted);font-size:.85rem;line-height:1.5;margin-top:.55rem}</style><figure class="c3ph-hero nb-hero" style=""><div class="c3ph-f"><img src="/images/buyers/no-hoa/garden-city-beach-and-marsh-from-the-ocean-2011-1200w.webp" srcset="/images/buyers/no-hoa/garden-city-beach-and-marsh-from-the-ocean-2011-600w.webp 600w, /images/buyers/no-hoa/garden-city-beach-and-marsh-from-the-ocean-2011-1200w.webp 1200w" sizes="(max-width: 1099px) 100vw, 380px" width="1200" height="782" alt="Beach houses in rows between the ocean beach and a wide marsh with tidal creeks and boat docks at Garden City Beach, seen from a plane over the ocean" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><span class="c3ph-cr"><a href="https://www.usa.gov/publicdomain/label/1.0/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" aria-label="Photo: U.S. Geological Survey. License: Public domain" title="License: Public domain">Photo: U.S. Geological Survey</a></span></div><figcaption>Garden City Beach from over the ocean: the oceanfront row of houses, two more rows behind it, and the salt marsh behind them.</figcaption></figure></div><p style="color:var(--muted);font-size:.9rem;margin-bottom:1rem">By <strong style="color:var(--navy);font-weight:600">Devin Day</strong>, Operations Officer &middot; Reviewed by <strong style="color:var(--navy);font-weight:600">Tim Nash</strong>, Broker-in-Charge &middot; <span style="white-space:nowrap">Updated November 8, 2026</span></p><p class="detail-sub">Where the houses a walk from the sand are, what they cost by distance from the ocean, the walk to a public beach access, and the flood zone.</p></div></div><section style="background:var(--ivory)"><div class="wrap"><p style="font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.7rem;letter-spacing:.14em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--brass);margin-bottom:.5rem;font-weight:600">The short answer</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Most houses for sale a short walk from the sand are in North Myrtle Beach, Myrtle Beach, and from Surfside Beach to Murrells Inlet. In the last year, a Horry County house within half a mile of the ocean sold for about $675,000 at the middle. Two to 5 miles inland, the middle sale was about $390,000.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">The price is highest in the first quarter mile from the ocean, where houses sold for about $805,000. A quarter to half a mile back, about a 10-minute walk or less, houses sold for about $540,000. About 1 in 4 houses there is in FEMA's high-risk flood zone, against about half nearer the ocean. Our map shows <a href="/homes/map/?q=house%20near%20the%20beach" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">the houses near the beach for sale today</a>.</p></div></section><section style="background:var(--navy);padding:3rem 0"><div class="wrap" style="text-align:center;max-width:720px;margin:0 auto"><p style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--ivory);margin-bottom:1rem">Tell us your budget and how far you will walk. We send the houses that fit.</p><a class="btn btn-brass btn-lg" href="/contact/">Send us your budget</a></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory);padding-top:2.5rem"><div class="wrap"><nav aria-label="On this page" style="margin-top:0;max-width:720px"><p style="font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.7rem;letter-spacing:.14em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--brass);margin-bottom:.3rem;font-weight:600">On this page</p><ul style="list-style:none;margin:0;padding:0"><li><a href="#cost" style="display:block;padding:.65rem 0;color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline;text-underline-offset:.18em;line-height:1.35">What they cost</a></li><li><a href="#walk" style="display:block;padding:.65rem 0;color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline;text-underline-offset:.18em;line-height:1.35">The walk</a></li><li><a href="#under-400k" style="display:block;padding:.65rem 0;color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline;text-underline-offset:.18em;line-height:1.35">Under $400,000</a></li><li><a href="#flood" style="display:block;padding:.65rem 0;color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline;text-underline-offset:.18em;line-height:1.35">Flood zones</a></li><li><a href="#towns" style="display:block;padding:.65rem 0;color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline;text-underline-offset:.18em;line-height:1.35">The beach towns</a></li><li><a href="#pros-cons" style="display:block;padding:.65rem 0;color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline;text-underline-offset:.18em;line-height:1.35">Pros and cons</a></li><li><a href="#houses-near-the-beach-faq" style="display:block;padding:.65rem 0;color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline;text-underline-offset:.18em;line-height:1.35">Houses near the beach FAQ</a></li></ul></nav></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory-2)" id="cost"><div class="wrap"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3" data-toc="What they cost">How much does a house near the beach cost in Myrtle Beach?</h2><div class="nb-side"><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">In the last year, Horry County houses within a quarter mile of the ocean sold for about $805,000 at the middle. Half sold for more and half for less.</p><div class="nb-aside"><style>main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact{padding-top:1rem;padding-bottom:.85rem}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact .cap{margin-bottom:.7rem}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact [role=rowgroup]{gap:.5rem}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact [role=row]{gap:.1rem .9rem}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact [role=rowheader]{line-height:1.3}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact .b{height:.5rem;min-width:.5rem}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact .v{line-height:1.25}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact figcaption{margin-top:.8rem}@media (max-width:699px){main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact [role=rowgroup]{gap:.45rem}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact [role=row]{gap:.05rem}}</style><figure class="c3-gchart c3-gchart-compact"><div role="table" aria-label="What a house sold for, by distance from the ocean"><span class="cap" aria-hidden="true">What a house sold for, by distance from the ocean</span><div role="rowgroup" class="sr"><div role="row"><span role="columnheader">Distance from the ocean</span><span role="columnheader">Middle sale price</span></div></div><div role="rowgroup"><div role="row"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">Under a quarter mile</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:1" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">$805,000</span></span></div><div role="row"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">A quarter to half a mile</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.671" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">$540,000</span></span></div><div role="row"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">Half a mile to 1 mile</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.634" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">$510,000</span></span></div><div role="row"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">1 to 2 miles</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.621" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">$500,000</span></span></div><div role="row" class="ref"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">2 to 5 miles</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.484" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">$390,000</span></span></div><div role="row" class="ref"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">5 to 10 miles</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.435" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">$350,000</span></span></div><div role="row" class="ref"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">10 miles or more</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.36" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">$290,000</span></span></div></div></div><figcaption>Houses sold in Horry County in the last year, from the county's deed records. The middle price: half sold for more, half for less. Gray bars: 2 miles or more inland.</figcaption></figure></div><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Houses a quarter mile to 2 miles back sold for about $500,000 to $540,000 at the middle. Houses 2 to 5 miles inland sold for about $390,000.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">A beach house within about a tenth of a mile of the ocean, about 500 feet, sold for about $1.33 million at the middle. From a tenth to a quarter mile, houses sold for about $705,000. Our <a href="/buyers/waterfront-homes/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">waterfront homes page</a> covers houses on the ocean itself.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Houses for sale today ask more per square foot the nearer they are to the ocean: about $445 within a quarter mile, $330 a quarter to half a mile back, and $220 two to 5 miles inland.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Within a quarter mile, the middle house for sale has about 2,350 square feet, against about 2,100 two to 5 miles inland. A quarter to half a mile back, it has about 1,800.</p></div></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory)" id="walk"><div class="wrap"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3" data-toc="The walk">How far is the walk to the beach from a house near the beach?</h2><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">We measured the walk to the sand from 721 houses for sale within 1.5 miles of the ocean. Each walk follows mapped streets and paths to the nearest public beach access on the state's map.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">At about 3 miles an hour, a quarter mile takes about 5 minutes on foot and half a mile about 10.</p><div class="nb-stat"><p class="k">The walk from houses for sale to the nearest public beach access</p><ul><li><strong>186 houses</strong><span>under a quarter mile on foot, about a 5-minute walk. Middle asking price about $950,000.</span></li><li><strong>109 houses</strong><span>a quarter to half a mile, about 10 minutes. Middle asking price about $680,000.</span></li><li><strong>104 houses</strong><span>half a mile to a mile on foot. Middle asking price about $650,000.</span></li></ul></div><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">A house that looks close on a map can be a long walk. Of the 356 houses for sale within half a mile of the ocean in a straight line, 27 are more than a mile on foot from a public access.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">The beach towns have a public path to the sand every few hundred feet. North Myrtle Beach manages over 240 beach accesses, and Myrtle Beach has 143. On the state's older map, which shows fewer, there is one about every 250 feet in North Myrtle Beach and every 350 to 400 feet in Myrtle Beach, Surfside Beach and Garden City.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">For a Horry County house within half a mile of the ocean, the nearest public access is about 1,000 feet away in a straight line at the middle.</p><ul class="nb-plain" aria-label="Three words in beach listings"><li><b>East of 17</b>In Myrtle Beach, the streets between Kings Highway, which is US 17 Business, and the ocean. Houses marked East of 17 in our home search are about 0.45 mile from the ocean at the middle.</li><li><b>Second row</b>The row of houses just behind the oceanfront row.</li><li><b>Walk to the beach</b>In our home search, houses marked walk to the beach are about a quarter mile from the ocean at the middle, and 9 in 10 are within about half a mile. Houses marked near the beach are about 0.73 mile out at the middle, and 9 in 10 are within about 2 miles.</li></ul><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Parking at the beach, resident passes and the beach rules are on our <a href="/buyers/relocating/beaches/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">page on the beaches</a>.</p><div style="border-left:3px solid var(--brass);background:var(--ivory-2);padding:1.2rem 1.4rem;margin:1.8rem 0;max-width:720px"><p style="color:var(--navy);font-weight:600;margin-bottom:.4rem">Is the beach really a short walk from that house?</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.7;margin-bottom:.8rem">Send us the listing. We measure the walk to the nearest public beach access and look up the flood zone the house is in.</p><a class="btn btn-brass" href="/contact/">Have us measure the walk</a></div></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory-2)" id="under-400k"><div class="wrap"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3" data-toc="Under $400,000">Where can you buy a house near the beach for under $400,000?</h2><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">About 1 in 6 house sales within half a mile of the ocean was under $400,000 in the last year: 72 of 450. Of those, 49 were in North Myrtle Beach and Cherry Grove, 18 in Myrtle Beach and 5 from Surfside Beach to Murrells Inlet.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">For sale today, 20 houses under $400,000 are a 10-minute walk or less from a public beach access. Fourteen of them are in North Myrtle Beach and Cherry Grove, 5 in Myrtle Beach and 1 from Surfside Beach to Murrells Inlet.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Our map shows <a href="/homes/map/?type=house&amp;has=walk_to_beach&amp;max=400000" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">the houses under $400,000 marked walk to the beach</a>.</p></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory)" id="flood"><div class="wrap"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3" data-toc="Flood zones">Will you need flood insurance for a house near the beach?</h2><div class="nb-side"><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Often, if the house is close to the ocean and you buy with a mortgage. About half of Horry County houses within a quarter mile of the ocean are in FEMA's high-risk flood zone. A quarter to half a mile back, about 1 in 4 are.</p><div class="nb-aside"><figure class="c3-gchart nb-fig"><span class="cap nb-cap">Share of houses in the high-risk flood zone, by distance from the ocean</span><svg class="nb-cols" viewBox="0 0 360 230" width="100%" role="img" aria-label="Column chart of the share of Horry County houses in FEMA's high-risk flood zone, by distance from the ocean in twentieths of a mile: 0.0 to 0.1 mile, 74 percent; 0.05 to 0.1 mile, 72 percent; 0.1 to 0.2 mile, 52 percent; 0.15 to 0.2 mile, 44 percent; 0.2 to 0.3 mile, 41 percent; 0.25 to 0.3 mile, 36 percent; 0.3 to 0.4 mile, 27 percent; 0.35 to 0.4 mile, 19 percent; 0.4 to 0.5 mile, 12 percent; 0.45 to 0.5 mile, 17 percent; 0.5 to 0.6 mile, 15 percent; 0.55 to 0.6 mile, 14 percent; 0.6 to 0.7 mile, 9 percent; 0.65 to 0.7 mile, 10 percent; 0.7 to 0.8 mile, 9 percent; 0.75 to 0.8 mile, 5 percent; 0.8 to 0.9 mile, 3 percent; 0.85 to 0.9 mile, 1 percent; 0.9 to 1 mile, 1 percent; 0.95 to 1 mile, 1 percent."><line x1="40" x2="352" y1="186" y2="186" stroke="#1c2028" stroke-opacity=".35"/><text x="34" y="191" text-anchor="end">0%</text><line x1="40" x2="352" y1="132.3" y2="132.3" stroke="#1c2028" stroke-opacity=".1"/><text x="34" y="137.3" text-anchor="end">25%</text><line x1="40" x2="352" y1="78.5" y2="78.5" stroke="#1c2028" stroke-opacity=".1"/><text x="34" y="83.5" text-anchor="end">50%</text><line x1="40" x2="352" y1="24.8" y2="24.8" stroke="#1c2028" stroke-opacity=".1"/><text x="34" y="29.8" text-anchor="end">75%</text><rect x="41.9" y="26.7" width="11.9" height="159.3" rx="2" fill="#c4783a"/><rect x="57.5" y="32.3" width="11.9" height="153.7" rx="2" fill="#c4783a"/><rect x="73.1" y="74.8" width="11.9" height="111.2" rx="2" fill="#c4783a"/><rect x="88.7" y="90.5" width="11.9" height="95.5" rx="2" fill="#c4783a"/><rect x="104.3" y="97" width="11.9" height="89" rx="2" fill="#c4783a"/><rect x="119.9" y="108.8" width="11.9" height="77.2" rx="2" fill="#c4783a"/><rect x="135.5" y="128.8" width="11.9" height="57.2" rx="2" fill="#c4783a"/><rect x="151.1" y="145.6" width="11.9" height="40.4" rx="2" fill="#c4783a"/><rect x="166.7" y="159.3" width="11.9" height="26.7" rx="2" fill="#c4783a"/><rect x="182.3" y="148.8" width="11.9" height="37.2" rx="2" fill="#c4783a"/><rect x="197.9" y="154.8" width="11.9" height="31.2" rx="2" fill="#d9b48f"/><rect x="213.5" y="155.9" width="11.9" height="30.1" rx="2" fill="#d9b48f"/><rect x="229.1" y="166" width="11.9" height="20" rx="2" fill="#d9b48f"/><rect x="244.7" y="164.5" width="11.9" height="21.5" rx="2" fill="#d9b48f"/><rect x="260.3" y="166.4" width="11.9" height="19.6" rx="2" fill="#d9b48f"/><rect x="275.9" y="176.1" width="11.9" height="9.9" rx="2" fill="#d9b48f"/><rect x="291.5" y="180.6" width="11.9" height="5.4" rx="2" fill="#d9b48f"/><rect x="307.1" y="184.1" width="11.9" height="1.9" rx="2" fill="#d9b48f"/><rect x="322.7" y="184.7" width="11.9" height="1.3" rx="2" fill="#d9b48f"/><rect x="338.3" y="183.6" width="11.9" height="2.4" rx="2" fill="#d9b48f"/><line x1="40" x2="40" y1="186" y2="191" stroke="#1c2028" stroke-opacity=".35"/><text x="40" y="208" text-anchor="start">0</text><line x1="118" x2="118" y1="186" y2="191" stroke="#1c2028" stroke-opacity=".35"/><text x="118" y="208" text-anchor="middle">¼</text><line x1="196" x2="196" y1="186" y2="191" stroke="#1c2028" stroke-opacity=".35"/><text x="196" y="208" text-anchor="middle">½</text><line x1="274" x2="274" y1="186" y2="191" stroke="#1c2028" stroke-opacity=".35"/><text x="274" y="208" text-anchor="middle">¾</text><line x1="352" x2="352" y1="186" y2="191" stroke="#1c2028" stroke-opacity=".35"/><text x="352" y="208" text-anchor="end">1 mile</text><text x="196" y="226" text-anchor="middle">Distance from the ocean</text></svg><figcaption>Each column is a twentieth of a mile, about 260 feet. Darker: the first half mile. Horry County houses, with FEMA's flood zones from the county's map, at the middle of each lot.</figcaption></figure></div><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">The high-risk zone is any A, AE or VE zone on the federal flood map. A federally backed or regulated mortgage on a home in a high-risk zone requires flood insurance.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">VE is the zone at the ocean edge where waves add to the risk. Fewer than 1 in 50 houses within half a mile of the ocean are in it.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">The share of houses in the high-risk zone drops below 1 in 10 between about 0.6 and 0.75 mile from the ocean. From about 0.85 mile, it is about 1 in 100.</p></div><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Near the ocean, the flood zone depends on the stretch of coast. Within half a mile, about 1 in 11 houses on the Myrtle Beach stretch is in the high-risk zone. In North Myrtle Beach and Cherry Grove it is about 4 in 10, and from Surfside Beach to Murrells Inlet about half.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">For a house the owner lives in, a FEMA flood policy in Horry County cost about $1,070 a year at the middle inside the high-risk zone, and about $550 outside it. For a house the owner does not live in, it was about $1,370 inside the zone.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Our <a href="/buyers/coastal-insurance/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">coastal insurance page</a> covers wind and flood policies here. Our <a href="/buyers/undisclosed-flooding/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">page on undisclosed flooding</a> covers what we look up to learn whether one house has flooded before.</p><div style="border-left:3px solid var(--brass);background:var(--ivory-2);padding:1.2rem 1.4rem;margin:1.8rem 0;max-width:720px"><p style="color:var(--navy);font-weight:600;margin-bottom:.4rem">Want a house near the sand and outside the high-risk flood zone?</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.7;margin-bottom:.8rem">Tell us the town. We send the houses for sale there that are outside FEMA's high-risk zone, with the walk to the beach from each.</p><a class="btn btn-brass" href="/contact/">Have us find them</a></div></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory-2)" id="towns"><div class="wrap"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3" data-toc="The beach towns">Which beach town near Myrtle Beach fits you?</h2><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">The coast from Cherry Grove to Pawleys Island is four stretches of beach towns, one after another. Here they are from north to south.</p><figure class="nb-mapfig"><div class="nb-mapframe"><svg class="nb-map" viewBox="0 0 1000 284" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" role="img" aria-labelledby="nb-map-t"><title id="nb-map-t">Map of the coast from Pawleys Island at the left to Cherry Grove at the right, turned so the shore runs across. A shaded strip along the shore is the land within half a mile of the ocean. Dots along the shore are public beach accesses: close together from Garden City to Cherry Grove, far apart at the two state parks and on Pawleys Island. Numbers mark the four stretches: 1 North Myrtle Beach and Cherry Grove, 2 Myrtle Beach, 3 Surfside Beach, Garden City and Murrells Inlet, 4 Litchfield and Pawleys Island.</title><rect width="1000" height="284" fill="#fbf8f3"/><path d="M24.5 234.4L31.4 231.7L34.3 230L40.8 228.2L42.5 226.7L43.2 225L45.2 222.8L48.1 221.2L49.1 220.1L56.6 215.4L59.5 215.4L61.6 214.7L76 207.7L82.9 203.5L85.6 201.1L94.8 194.2L105.2 186.9L109.6 184.1L118.5 179.5L125.5 177.2L132.1 174.3L136.4 173.2L140.9 171.2L185.8 156.4L198.4 153.8L200 152.9L204.4 152L213.6 148.5L224 145.7L239.9 142.3L246.1 141.2L262.5 139.7L274.4 139.9L281.1 140.5L290.2 140.2L292.9 140.5L305.8 140.7L307.8 141.1L309.3 140.9L317.2 137.8L320.5 137.1L328 138.6L329.9 140.1L332.1 140.2L341.2 138.2L347.1 135.5L353.1 133.3L361.2 131L376.7 127.6L388.1 126.2L392.7 126.1L397.4 125.1L403.6 124.9L424 122.7L427.8 122.6L432.1 121.8L452 120.1L458.1 119L479.3 117.4L480.1 117.1L481.5 117.3L490.9 116.6L518.3 116.9L523.1 116.6L524.5 116.1L527 115.9L554 116.5L553.9 117.2L554.8 117.2L554.9 116.4L558.6 116.5L558.6 117.4L560.7 116.9L567.3 117.4L567.3 117.7L567.8 117.7L567.7 117.3L577.3 116.3L577.4 116.7L579.3 116.5L579.3 116.1L596.3 115.7L632 117.2L638.6 117.9L638.8 118.2L638.8 117.9L641.9 118.4L648.9 118.5L648.9 118.9L649.2 118.5L653 118.9L653 119.3L659.9 119.3L678.7 121.9L679.1 122.3L681.8 122.6L681.8 122.2L684.1 122.9L687.3 123.3L687.3 123L695 124L698.7 125.3L722.2 129.3L727.6 130.8L748.2 135.5L752.8 136L759.4 138.1L767.9 139.7L792.3 145.9L817 154.1L825.1 157.2L856.5 170.8L874.7 180.7L885.8 185.1L891.7 187.9L905.3 195.6L909.3 197.3L909.5 196.8L911.9 199.2L920.2 202.9L923 203.6L924.9 204.7L936 212.2L940 215.7L947.2 220.8L948.1 222.9L950.1 224.6L951.2 224.9L953.8 224.3L954.2 225.7L954.8 225.8L963.2 230.5L975.5 234.4L1000 234.4L1000 284L0 284L0 234.4Z" fill="#d3e0e5"/><path d="M24.5 234.4L31.4 231.7L34.3 230L40.8 228.2L42.5 226.7L